=== AGENTS.md
<!-- BEGIN:yuanme -->
<!-- Written by yuanme [version], which rewrites this block when another version runs here. Write your own notes outside it. -->

# yuanme

This project is a Site that yuanme builds: a static site generator for Markdown and Org, with math. `yuanme.toml` is the Site config, Entries are Markdown or Org files in `content/`, and Templates are Jinja files in `templates/`.

## Work loop

1. Edit the files.
2. Run `yuanme check --json`. Each line it prints is one JSON event. A `diagnostic` has a `code`, the place in a file, and often a fix: apply a suggestion whose `applicability` is `machine-applicable` as it is, and for any other, read `yuanme docs CODE` and fix what the code names.
3. Repeat until `check` exits 0. Exit 1 means the Site has errors, and 2 that the command itself was wrong.
4. To see the Pages, run `yuanme dev --background --json`. It returns after the first build, with a `server-ready` event that holds the URL: never assume the port. `yuanme dev status --json` says whether a dev server runs and how its last build went, `.yuanme/dev.json` says where it runs, `.yuanme/dev.log` holds what it printed, and `yuanme dev stop` stops it.
5. `yuanme build --json` writes the Site, and `.yuanme/report.md`, which measures each Page against the Site budgets.

More commands that print JSON with `--json`:

- `yuanme routes`: every URL, and the Entry or Template that makes it.
- `yuanme new COLLECTION "Title"`: a new Entry with its required fields filled in.
- `yuanme schema config`, `entry COLLECTION`, `data NAME` or `context KIND`: the JSON Schema of Site config, a Collection's front matter, a Data file, or what a kind of Route's Template sees. `.yuanme/schemas/` holds them too.

## Rules agents get wrong

- An Entry's body is Markdown or Org, never Jinja: `{{ }}` and `{% %}` in a body are text. Logic goes in Templates.
- Org outside the Org subset is an error, never dropped. `yuanme docs org` lists the subset.
- Label an equation with `\label{eq:name}` inside its math, and cite it with `\eqref{eq:name}`, in both Source formats. A link with no text to a Label, `[](#thm:name)` in Markdown or `[[thm:name]]` in Org, shows the target's number.
- A key that Site config or a Collection doesn't declare is an error, and the help names the key meant. Read the schema rather than guessing.
- Never edit `.yuanme/`: yuanme rewrites everything in it.
- A Page over a Site budget is a warning. Make the Page smaller before you acknowledge it in `[budgets.overages]`.

## Docs

These pages are for this version of yuanme. Read the one for a task before you start it; `yuanme docs NAME` prints the same.

- `.yuanme/docs/getting-started.md`: Install yuanme, make a Site with one Post, check it and build it.
- `.yuanme/docs/config.md`: yuanme.toml, the one file that declares the Site, with every key it takes.
- `.yuanme/docs/collections.md`: Collections and their Entries, the fields every Entry has and the ones a Collection declares, Slugs, Taxonomies, Data files, and yuanme new.
- `.yuanme/docs/markdown.md`: The Markdown yuanme reads: CommonMark with GFM, heading ids and Labels, links between Entries, raw HTML, code blocks and ::: blocks.
- `.yuanme/docs/org.md`: How an Org file becomes an Entry, which Org yuanme renders, what it rejects or warns about, and where it differs from Emacs.
- `.yuanme/docs/math.md`: LaTeX math in Markdown and Org, rendered to MathML at build time, with numbered equations, Labels, references and macros.
- `.yuanme/docs/templates.md`: The Jinja files that make each Page, what each kind of Route sees, the filters yuanme adds, Layouts and Partials, and what check finds in them.
- `.yuanme/docs/components.md`: Reusable pieces of Templates with declared props, how to call them, how they differ from Partials, and the Sidecars beside them.
- `.yuanme/docs/styles.md`: Link stylesheets from a Template; yuanme bundles their imports, runs Tailwind for one that imports it, adds prefixes for your browsers, minifies and hashes them, and copies Static files as they are.
- `.yuanme/docs/scripts.md`: Load TypeScript or JavaScript modules from a Template; yuanme bundles them, with packages from node_modules, into minified and hashed chunks.
- `.yuanme/docs/images.md`: How Entry bodies name images, what yuanme makes of them, the image field type, and the [images] settings.
- `.yuanme/docs/deploying.md`: What yuanme build writes, the Host adapter for each static host, the cache policy, headers, redirects and the 404 Page.
- `.yuanme/docs/cli.md`: Every command and flag, the exit codes, and the JSON that --json prints.
- `.yuanme/docs/budgets.md`: The Site budgets yuanme build measures every Page against, how to change them, strict mode, and the build report.

Each Diagnostic code has a page too, such as `.yuanme/docs/entry/unknown-key.md` for `entry/unknown-key`.
<!-- END:yuanme -->
